# Curated conversational synonyms for the RAG lexical retriever.
# Loaded once at startup by LuceneAnalyzers via SolrSynonymParser and
# applied as a query-time SynonymGraphFilter so the index stays
# rebuild-free when this file changes.
#
# Solr format:
#   - lines starting with # are comments
#   - blank lines are ignored
#   - `a, b, c` means bidirectional equivalence: any of {a,b,c}
#     matches all others
#   - `a, b => c, d` means one-directional: {a,b} in the query
#     expand to {c,d} (not the reverse)
#
# Editing policy:
#   - Sections are organised by the four current target personas
#     (consulting, recruiting, UX research, sales/AM) plus
#     cross-cutting terms every persona shares. Grow the section
#     for the persona that produced the failing query, not a
#     generic "misc" bucket.
#   - Every synonym is a potential false positive; err on the side
#     of NOT adding vs adding aggressively, especially for 2-3
#     letter abbreviations ('sql', 'arr', 'cac') that can collide
#     across domains.
#   - Multi-word entries need a space, no quotes. Stopwords inside
#     multi-word phrases are stripped by the analyzer at load time
#     (so 'statement of work' -> 'statement work' in the map,
#     matching a chunk that says 'statement of work' for the same
#     reason).
#   - All entries are lowercase to match the analyzer output; the
#     synonym filter runs AFTER LowerCaseFilter + ASCIIFoldingFilter
#     but BEFORE EnglishMinimalStemFilter, so use the base singular
#     form and let the stemmer handle plurals downstream.
#   - Test against a real transcript before shipping.

